The Food and Nutrition class at a secondary school in Jamaica has been asked to prepare and serve a two-course dinner for 20 guests at the school's graduation ceremony. The dinner will be served at 7:00 p.m. in the school's food laboratory, and the class has $18 000 to spend on the food.

Among the guests are:
- Mr Clarke, an 82-year-old man who has diabetes mellitus and hypertension and who wears dentures;
- a married couple who are lacto-ovo vegetarians;
- four students who are athletes in training.

The class must hand a written menu to the teacher before they shop for the food.
